---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SpecTable from '../components/SpecTable.astro';
import Todo from '../components/Todo.astro';
import { site } from '../site';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Background, working approach, languages and education of Houssam Boudiar, a full-stack engineer in Algiers who is open to relocation."
>
  <div class="wrap section about">
    <div class="prose">
      <span class="hud">About</span>
      <h1>Background</h1>
      <p>
        I'm a full-stack engineer based in Algiers. I studied computer science at the University of
        Constantine 2 and finished an MSc in Software Engineering in 2020.
      </p>
      <p>
        Since March 2022 I've worked at Smartest in Algiers on two products: a well integrity
        management system for the oil &amp; gas sector, and Mobility One, a ticketing platform for
        public transport. Both run on-premise, often offline, for customers who care a lot about who
        can see and change what. In that time I've worked across the whole stack, from the
        Angular and React frontends to NestJS and FastAPI services, PostgreSQL, Keycloak and the
        LLM agent layer.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm looking for full-stack or AI engineering roles and I'm open to relocation.
        <Todo note="add notice period / earliest start date if you want it shown" />
      </p>

      <h2>How I work</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Hard rules go in code, not in prompts.</strong> When an LLM can act, I limit what
          it can reach with permission-scoped tools, enforced limits and approval steps, so
          a persuasive prompt can't change what it's allowed to do.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Agree on contracts early.</strong> A shared OpenAPI spec, a generated client and
          shared validation rules let frontend and backend teams move in parallel without guessing.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Test what is expensive to fix later.</strong> On-premise software is hard to
          patch once it ships, so I write end-to-end tests that include accessibility and
          right-to-left layout checks.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Failures should be visible.</strong> Alarms that must be acknowledged, audit logs,
          and model fallbacks that say they are fallbacks. A degraded result should never look
          like a good one.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="facts">
      <section aria-labelledby="lang-heading">
        <h2 id="lang-heading" class="hud facts__h">Languages</h2>
        <SpecTable
          rows={[
            ['Arabic', 'Native'],
            ['English', 'C1 (IELTS)'],
            ['French', 'B2'],
            ['German', 'A2'],
          ]}
        />
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="edu-heading">
        <h2 id="edu-heading" class="hud facts__h">Education</h2>
        <SpecTable
          rows={[
            ['2020', 'MSc Software Engineering, University of Constantine 2 – Abdelhamid Mehri'],
            ['2018', 'BSc Computer Science, University of Constantine 2 – Abdelhamid Mehri'],
          ]}
        />
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="exp-heading">
        <h2 id="exp-heading" class="hud facts__h">Experience</h2>
        <SpecTable rows={[['2022 –', 'Full-Stack Developer, Smartest, Algiers']]} />
      </section>
      <p>
        <a class="btn" href={site.cv}>Full CV <span class="sr-only">(PDF)</span><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .about {
    display: grid;
    gap: 3rem;
  }
  @media (min-width: 64rem) {
    .about {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 22rem;
      align-items: start;
    }
  }
  .facts {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem;
  }
  .facts__h {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
  }
</style>
